\section{Creating and deleting}
To make a file or directory the code needs a run of free entries in the directory: one for the short name plus the pieces of the long name (FAT32), or the whole set (exFAT). Free entries are the deleted ones and everything after the end mark; if the
chain is full a new cluster is added to the directory.

\paragraph{FAT32 short names.} A long name needs a short name, too, and it must be unique in the directory. If the long name is an upper case 8.3 name already, it is the short name and there are no extra entries.
Otherwise the short name is the first six letters of the name (upper case, illegal characters replaced by an underscore), then [[~1]], [[~2]] \ldots{} until it is unique, and the extension. The long name is
stored in pieces of 13 characters, each with the checksum of the short name, so that a program that knows only short names still sees the file, and a damaged chain of pieces is recognised.

\paragraph{exFAT sets.} The first entry has the number of secondary entries and a checksum over the whole set (a 16 bit rotation sum, without the checksum field itself); the stream extension has the name length and a hash of the upper case name.

